# Peanut Chicken Zucchini Noodles

Based on [sallysbakingaddiction.com](https://sallysbakingaddiction.com/peanut-chicken-zucchini-noodles) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251114233417/https://sallysbakingaddiction.com/peanut-chicken-zucchini-noodles/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 2 Tbsps [sesame oil]{ ing="sesame-oil" } (for vegetables)
- [ ] 2 tsp [minced or chopped garlic]{ ing="minced-or-chopped-garlic" }
- [ ] 1 cup [shredded carrots]{ ing="shredded-carrots" }
- [ ] 1 cup [thinly sliced cabbage]{ ing="thinly-sliced-cabbage" } (red recommended)
- [ ] 1 large [bell pepper]{ ing="bell-pepper" }, thinly sliced (red recommended)
- [ ] 1.5 lbs (680g) [zucchini]{ ing="zucchini" }, spiralized into noodles
- [ ] 2 large [chicken breasts]{ ing="chicken-breasts" }, cooked and shredded (about 2-3 cups)

### Peanut Sauce

- [ ] 1/2 cup [creamy peanut butter]{ ing="creamy-peanut-butter" }
- [ ] 1/3 cup [honey]{ ing="honey" }
- [ ] 1/3 cup [soy sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" } (reduced sodium preferred)
- [ ] 2 Tbsps [sesame oil]{ ing="sesame-oil" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsps [rice vinegar]{ ing="rice-vinegar" }
- [ ] 2 tsp fresh [ginger]{ ing="ginger" }, minced
- [ ] 1-2 tsp Sriracha or [hot chile sauce]{ ing="hot-chile-sauce" }

### Optional Toppings

- [ ] 1 Tbsp [sesame seeds]{ ing="sesame-seeds" }
- [ ] [Cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup [peanuts]{ ing="peanuts" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [chopped green onion]{ ing="chopped-green-onion" }

## Recipe

1. Heat 2 Tbsps [sesame oil]{ ing="sesame-oil" } and [garlic]{ ing="minced-or-chopped-garlic" } in a large skillet over medium heat. Add [carrots]{ ing="shredded-carrots" }, [cabbage]{ ing="thinly-sliced-cabbage" }, and [pepper]{ ing="bell-pepper" }. Cook approximately 5 minutes until tender. Meanwhile, prepare the [peanut]{ ing="peanuts" } [sauce]{ ing="hot-chile-sauce" }. Add [zucchini]{ ing="zucchini" } noodles and shredded chicken; cook and stir 3 minutes until zucchini softens and chicken warms. Remove from heat and set aside. Process in batches if skillet space is limited.
1. Combine all peanut sauce ingredients in a small saucepan over low heat. Whisk constantly until [peanut butter]{ ing="creamy-peanut-butter" } melts and everything combines. Adjust Sriracha to desired heat level.
1. Pour sauce over chicken and vegetables. Toss until combined. Plate and garnish with [sesame seeds]{ ing="sesame-seeds" }, [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, peanuts, and [green onion]{ ing="chopped-green-onion" }. Serve immediately.
1. Refrigerate leftovers for a few days. Reheat as preferred.

## Notes

- **Rice vinegar**: Essential for authentic flavor; avoid white wine or white vinegar due to harshness
- **Zucchini**: Pre-spiralized versions available in produce sections, or use a home spiralizer
- **Chicken**: Boil skinless boneless breasts for 12-15 minutes, or use rotisserie chicken, leftover cooked chicken, or substitute with beef, shrimp, salmon, or tofu
- **Ingredient substitutions**: Gluten-free soy sauce or coconut aminos work for soy sauce; almond butter replaces peanut butter for allergies; pasta or rice noodles can replace zucchini noodles
